# .trivyignore-cluster -- accepted CRITICAL CVEs for the platform's own images
# (images we deploy), enforced by `just cluster verify image-scan`, the
# image-security gate run from `local.yml`. DOKS-managed images (kube-system)
# are out of scope, and only CRITICAL is gated -- HIGH findings are
# visibility-only (trivy-operator dashboards + Renovate chart bumps), so they
# are not listed here.
#
# One CVE ID per line; `#` comments. Every entry needs a reason and a ROADMAP.md
# tracking item so it is removed once the chart ships a fixed image. Any new,
# unlisted CRITICAL in a platform image fails the gate.

# Go stdlib -- external-secrets bitwarden-sdk-server:v0.6.0 is built with a Go
# release predating the fix; no patched chart image is available yet. Renovate
# bumps the external-secrets chart when one ships. Tracked in ROADMAP.md.
CVE-2025-68121

# rancher/local-path-provisioner (path traversal via StorageClass
# parameters.pathPattern, fixed in v0.0.34) -- this is kind's own bundled
# default-StorageClass image, not something any chart or manifest in this repo
# pins; the fix ships only via a newer `kind` release picked up by bumping the
# Nix-pinned nixpkgs (`just update`), a separate, deliberate operation. Not
# shipped to users: it exists only on the ephemeral, single-tenant, torn-down-
# after-use kind clusters `local.yml`/`just cluster local` provision, which
# never grant an untrusted principal the StorageClass-creating API access this
# needs to exploit. Tracked in ROADMAP.md.
CVE-2025-62878

# proxy-addr (IP spoofing via IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnets, fixed upstream in
# proxy-addr 2.0.8) -- transitive via Express in mendhak/http-https-echo.
# Confirmed empirically: tag 42 (the latest, bumped from 41 for this) still
# bundles the vulnerable proxy-addr; the image doesn't pin its Express
# dependency tightly enough to have picked up the fix yet. Also not exploitable
# as configured: the vulnerable path requires an IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust-proxy
# subnet, and flux/echo/deployment.yaml sets TRUST_PROXY=true (trust all), not
# a subnet list. Disposable CI test backend regardless, never user-facing.
# Tracked in ROADMAP.md.
CVE-2026-90711
